(they throw upon the character of this movement. The method employed in) Tj T*
(this investigation has been largely statistical and comparative, a) Tj T*
(fact which is partly due to the kind of material that was available) Tj T*
(and partly to the point of view that has been taken. Certain economic) Tj T*
(and social factors, having a close bearing upon the past and present) Tj T*
(situation of the Jews in Eastern Europe and frequently neglected in) Tj T*
(the discussion of the various phases of this movement, have been) Tj T*
(emphasized in the examination into the causes of the emigration of the) Tj T*
(Jews from Eastern Europe and have been found vital in determining the) Tj T*
(specific character of the Jewish immigration to this country.) Tj T*
