(CHAPTER III) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE JEWS IN EASTERN EUROPE: ECONOMIC AND SOCIAL POSITION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The economic and social life of the Jews in Eastern Europe has moved) Tj T*
(along the familiar channels of commerce, industry and urban life) Tj T*
(characteristic of the Jews in all countries during the middle ages. An) Tj T*
(examination of the economic position and function and the principal) Tj T*
(social characteristics of the Jews reveals the fact that they play an) Tj T*
(important part in each of these countries. This we shall see by) Tj T*
(tracing their principal economic activities and some significant) Tj T*
(phases of their social life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I. RUSSIA) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A review of the occupations of the Jews in the Russian Empire shows) Tj T*
(that those engaged in the manufacturing and mechanical pursuits) Tj T*
(constituted 39 per cent of the total Jewish population gainfully) Tj T*
(employed. This was the largest occupational group. Commerce engaged 32) Tj T*
(per cent. Together the industrial and commercial classes comprised) Tj T*
(seven-tenths of all Jews engaged in gainful occupations. On the other) Tj T*
(hand, only 3 per cent were employed in agricultural pursuits.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is in comparison with the occupations of the non-Jewish population) Tj T*
(in Russia that the significance of this distribution becomes evident.) Tj T*
(Of the non-Jews in Russia, agricultural pursuits engaged 61 per cent,) Tj T*
(manufacturing and mechanical pursuits 15 per cent, and commerce only 3) Tj T*
