(restrictive laws is unquestioned. The chief reason for this, however,) Tj T*
(is occupational. The Jews as an industrial and commercial people) Tj T*
(constitute one of the main elements out of which the town populations) Tj T*
(are recruited. Towns are ordinarily the foci of all the cultural) Tj T*
(forces and the movement and enterprise of a country. In Eastern) Tj T*
(Europe, where the number of towns is so few, this is much more the) Tj T*
(case than in Western Europe. The fact that the Jews are so largely) Tj T*
(concentrated in these comparatively few towns serves to give them a) Tj T*
(cultural position and influence far out of proportion to their) Tj T*
(numbers. Their economic activities and their relatively large) Tj T*
(participation in the liberal professions strengthens this position) Tj T*
(considerably.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
