(Religious intolerance had been the prime motive of Russia's policy of) Tj T*
(completely excluding the Jews from her borders. Through the partitions) Tj T*
(of Poland from 1772 to 1795, she became the unwilling ruler over the) Tj T*
(destinies of millions of Jews living in Lithuania, Western and) Tj T*
(Southwestern Russia and Poland proper. The historic medieval principle) Tj T*
(by which the Jews were regarded as an alien and heretic race living) Tj T*
(among the Christian peoples--a principle that had, with the growth of) Tj T*
(modern ideas, been rapidly losing its hold upon the West-European) Tj T*
(nations--expressed Russia's attitude towards the Jews and conformed to) Tj T*
(her strongly medieval outlook and organization of this period. Thus,) Tj T*
(at the time when the emancipation of the Jews had begun to be in) Tj T*
(Western Europe a concomitant of social progress, Russia set to work to) Tj T*
(recreate almost typically medieval conditions for a vaster Jewish) Tj T*
(population than had ever before been assembled in any European) Tj T*
(country.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Jews were placed in the position practically of aliens, whose) Tj T*
(activities were regulated by special laws. The first and the most) Tj T*
(far-reaching of these laws limited their right of residence to those) Tj T*
(provinces in which they lived at the time of the Polish partitions. In) Tj T*
(this way originated that reproduction on a vast scale of the medieval) Tj T*
(Ghetto--the Pale of Jewish Settlement. The elementary right of free) Tj T*
(movement and choice of residence, which was denied to the Jews, has) Tj T*
(remained the principal restriction to which they are subjected.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Pale of Jewish Settlement, continued with but few changes to our) Tj T*
(day, includes the fifteen provinces of Western and Southwestern) Tj T*
(Russia--Vilna, Kovno, Grodno, Minsk, Vitebsk, Mohileff, Volhynia,) Tj T*
