(It was at the famous Berlin Congress, convened to decide questions) Tj T*
(created by the Russo-Turkish war of 1877, that the subject of the) Tj T*
(Jewish disabilities in Roumania was brought up, in connection with the) Tj T*
(demand of Roumania for recognition as an independent state. The chief) Tj T*
(objection made especially by the representatives of three of the) Tj T*
(European powers--France, England and Germany--was Roumania's treatment) Tj T*
(of the Jews. It was finally decided by the Congress to recognize her) Tj T*
(independence on the condition that she grant civil and political) Tj T*
(equality to all her citizens without distinction of race or creed.) Tj T*
(This was expressed in Article 44 of the historic Berlin Treaty, which) Tj T*
(read as follows:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Article 44. In Roumania, difference in religious beliefs and) Tj T*
(    confessions shall not be brought against anyone as a ground for) Tj T*
(    exclusion or unfitness as regards the enjoyment of civil and) Tj T*
(    political rights, admission to public offices, functions, and) Tj T*
(    honors, or the exercise of various professions and industries in) Tj T*
(    any place whatever. Freedom in outward observance of all creeds) Tj T*
(    will be assured to all subjects of the Roumanian state, as well) Tj T*
(    as to strangers, and no obstacle will be raised either to the) Tj T*
(    ecclesiastical organization of different bodies, or to their) Tj T*
(    intercourse with their spiritual heads.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    The citizens of all states, whether merchants or others, shall) Tj T*
(    be dealt with, in Roumania, without distinction of religion, on) Tj T*
(    the basis of perfect equality.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the _constituante_ which was convoked soon after to discuss the) Tj T*
(question of giving the Jews equal political rights, an interesting) Tj T*
(picture is obtained of the sentiment of the upper and middle classes) Tj T*
(of Roumania.[40] An overwhelming majority was opposed to the granting) Tj T*
(of political rights to the Jews on the ground that Roumania was a) Tj T*
(Christian-Latin State, or on the purely nationalistic ground that the) Tj T*
(Jews were an alien and utterly unassimilable element of the) Tj T*
(population. To meet the demands of the Powers the principle of) Tj T*
(individual naturalization was adopted, by which an alien could be) Tj T*
(granted naturalization individually and only by a special vote of the) Tj T*
(Chamber of Deputies. Other onerous conditions, such as the) Tj T*
(requirement of a ten years' residence in the country for citizenship,) Tj T*
(and the prohibition of the purchase by aliens of rural estates, showed) Tj T*
(conclusively that Roumania was prepared to give only formal assent to) Tj T*
(the demand of the Powers.[41] After a year of negotiations, the three) Tj T*
(Powers agreed to the recognition of her independence, expressing the) Tj T*
(hope that the Roumanian government would recognize the inadequacy of) Tj T*
(the revised article and especially of the principle of individual) Tj T*
(naturalization as meeting the conditions of the Berlin Treaty, and) Tj T*
(would aim towards a complete emancipation of all her subjects.[42]) Tj T*
