(The great financial crash of 1873, in which several Jewish financial) Tj T*
(houses were concerned, was the starting-point of political) Tj T*
(antisemitism in Austria. The Jews were denounced as the) Tj T*
(representatives of the capitalist order of society, with its) Tj T*
(overwhelming concentration of wealth and its exploitation of the) Tj T*
(industrial and the agricultural proletariat. The Christian-Socialist) Tj T*
(movement began with antisemitism as the corner-stone of its economic) Tj T*
(and social doctrines. Its opposition to the Jews and to capitalism was) Tj T*
(largely due to medieval prejudices in favor of the Christian-feudal) Tj T*
(state and the medieval industrial organization. In the early eighties) Tj T*
(it began to triumph when the "small man" or petty industrialist) Tj T*
(received political power through an extension of the suffrage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It reached its height in the nineties, when, under the combined) Tj T*
(influence of feudal-clerical nobles, the clergy and the lower middle) Tj T*
(class, a period of reaction set in. In Vienna, in 1895, the antisemite) Tj T*
(Lueger was elected mayor. Powerless though they were to change the) Tj T*
(legal status of the Jews, the antisemites succeeded in creating in) Tj T*
(both upper and lower circles of Austrian society an atmosphere of) Tj T*
(antagonism to the Jews which has prevented the complete fulfillment of) Tj T*
(the principle of equality as set forth in the constitution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The clericals have fanned the flames of religious hatred especially) Tj T*
(among the peasantry by ritual-murder accusations, which have been rife) Tj T*
(and have played a large part in strengthening the sentiment of) Tj T*
(hostility toward the Jews.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
