(The industrial and commercial development of the recent decades) Tj T*
(brought about changes in themselves unfavorable to the economic) Tj T*
(activities of the Jews. The improvements in communication and) Tj T*
(transportation through the extension of railroads, the building of) Tj T*
(roads, and the creation of credit facilities especially for the) Tj T*
(peasantry served partly to displace the Jews, whose economic position) Tj T*
(had been largely based upon the services they rendered in a relatively) Tj T*
(backward industrial and commercial civilization. The rise of a middle) Tj T*
(class among the Christian populations, chiefly engaged in industry,) Tj T*
(added an element of competition not before present. Not the least) Tj T*
(important in its effects was the increasing poverty of the peasantry,) Tj T*
(which seriously affected the Jews, as the principal buyers of their) Tj T*
(produce and sellers of finished products. Agricultural crises, so) Tj T*
(frequent in recent years in Eastern Europe, have often involved the) Tj T*
(Jews in financial ruin.[47]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These purely economic factors served to weaken the position of the) Tj T*
(Jews and to cause an over-concentration in trade and industry, to) Tj T*
(their detriment. The gradual readjustment that would have followed) Tj T*
(naturally was, however, prevented by the existence of other forces, in) Tj T*
(the action of which we find the key to the situation faced by the Jews) Tj T*
(and the impelling forces of Jewish emigration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One of these was the economic antisemitism that rose partly from the) Tj T*
(competition of the middle classes of both populations. This) Tj T*
(competitive jealousy awakened racial and religious prejudices and) Tj T*
(found particularly in Galicia an active expression in the organization) Tj T*
(of economic boycotts, and in the co-operative agencies that were) Tj T*
(created to foster the growth of the Christian artisans and merchants.) Tj T*
(The sufferings of the agricultural population, again, were charged to) Tj T*
(the Jews, with whom the peasants were in close business relations and) Tj T*
(to whom they were deeply indebted. Preached from platform, press and) Tj T*
(pulpit, the doctrine of Jewish exploitation of the peasantry found a) Tj T*
(ready acceptance among all classes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Economic and social hostility was furthered by the feudal ruling) Tj T*
(classes whose antagonism to the Jews was deep-seated and many-sided.) Tj T*
(As these formed the ruling economic, social and political power in) Tj T*
(Eastern Europe, they were the chief instrument in creating a situation) Tj T*
(that was full of danger for the Jews. In the politico-economic) Tj T*
(struggles between these privileged classes and the liberal middle) Tj T*
(classes that accompanied the transition, the Jews were found,) Tj T*
(consciously or unconsciously, on the side of the liberals, who sought) Tj T*
(to introduce the economic, social and political conditions of modern) Tj T*
(civilization. Thus they served as a convenient object of attack. In) Tj T*
(Russia, where, since the reaction, the control of the feudal classes) Tj T*
(over the government was complete, the new laws restricting residence,) Tj T*
(movement, occupations and economic activity in general, checked the) Tj T*
(economic growth of the Jews and put them at a great disadvantage in) Tj T*
(the struggle for existence. This situation was created to an even) Tj T*
