(Hersch, \(_Le juif errant d'aujourd'hui_\), subjects the figures given) Tj T*
(in the _Jewish Encyclopedia_ to a thorough analysis and shows their) Tj T*
(absurdity. Unaware, however, of the nature of the error committed by) Tj T*
(the writer and of the existence of authoritative sources for the) Tj T*
(figures of Jewish immigration, he drew the conclusion that it is) Tj T*
(impossible to obtain any really accurate figures of Jewish immigration) Tj T*
(before 1899. This leads him into serious errors owing to the fact that) Tj T*
(he discusses the movement of Jewish immigration from the basis of the) Tj T*
(twelve years from 1899 to 1910, representing the height of the) Tj T*
(movement, instead of for the entire period of thirty years. This) Tj T*
(vitiates his principal conclusions regarding the character of the) Tj T*
(Jewish movement to this country. Particularly noticeable is his) Tj T*
(neglect of the phenomena presented by the Russian and Roumanian) Tj T*
(movements and his elevation of the movement from Austria-Hungary as) Tj T*
(the type of Jewish immigration to this country.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER II) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(IMMIGRATION OF JEWS FROM EASTERN EUROPE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the thirty years between 1881 and 1910, 1,562,800 Jews entered the) Tj T*
(United States. An examination of Tables VI and VII reveals the fact) Tj T*
(that the great majority of the immigrants came from Russia,) Tj T*
(Austria-Hungary and Roumania. Of the total number, Russia contributed) Tj T*
(1,119,059 immigrants, or 71.6 percent; Austria-Hungary 281,150) Tj T*
(immigrants, or 17.9 per cent, and Roumania 67,057 immigrants, or 4.3) Tj T*
(per cent. Together these three countries contributed 93.8 per cent of) Tj T*
(the total for the thirty years. The great majority of the Jewish) Tj T*
(immigrants from the United Kingdom and British North America are not) Tj T*
(English or Canadian Jews but transmigrants or transient East-European) Tj T*
