(Jewish immigrants from Russia maintained a fairly constant proportion) Tj T*
(to the total Jewish immigration, contributing 135,003, in the decade) Tj T*
(between 1881 and 1890 or 69.9 per cent of the total for the decade,) Tj T*
(279,811 or 71.1 per cent in the decade between 1891 and 1900, and) Tj T*
(704,245, or 72.1 per cent, in the decade between 1901 and 1910.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Roumanian Jewish immigration was relatively smaller in the earlier) Tj T*
(decades, numbering 6,967 in the first, 12,789 in the second decade,) Tj T*
