() Tj T*
(CHAPTER III) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(IMMIGRATION OF JEWS FROM RUSSIA) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The mass-movement of the Russian Jews to the United States began in) Tj T*
(the first year of Alexander III's reign. Though in this year the) Tj T*
(number of Russian Jews entering this country amounted to a little over) Tj T*
(three thousand, the immigration grew so rapidly and in such) Tj T*
(proportions that at the end of thirty years, more than a million) Tj T*
(Russian Jews had been admitted to the United States.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An examination of the figures of the Russian Jewish immigration for) Tj T*
(the thirty years[63] reveals that it is a movement of steady growth.) Tj T*
(The Russian Jewish immigration falls practically into two periods; the) Tj T*
(first culminating in 1892, the second culminating in 1906. Considering) Tj T*
(it by decades,[64] we find that the movement is one of geometrical) Tj T*
(progression. In the first decade, from 1881 to 1890, 135,003 Russian) Tj T*
(Jews entered the country, 12.1 per cent of the total Russian Jewish) Tj T*
(immigrants. Between 1891 and 1900, 279,811 Russian Jews entered,) Tj T*
(constituting 25.0 per cent of the total. In the last decade, from 1901) Tj T*
(to 1910, there entered 704,245 Russian Jews, or 62.9 per cent of the) Tj T*
(total.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The annual variations are, nevertheless, considerable and largely) Tj T*
(explainable by the special conditions in Russia that have influenced) Tj T*
(the lives of the Jews throughout this period. At the beginning of this) Tj T*
(period, in 1881, the immigration of Russian Jews was small. The) Tj T*
(_pogroms_ of 1881-2 were reflected in the sudden rise in 1882 to) Tj T*
(10,489 immigrants, more than three times the number of the preceding) Tj T*
(year. The immigration of this year was rather a flight than a normal) Tj T*
