(The progressive nature of the Jewish movement has been disclosed. The) Tj T*
(greatest numbers have come within the last decade. This is) Tj T*
(particularly true of the movement from Roumania, and to a less extent) Tj T*
(of the movement from Russia. On the other hand, a larger relative) Tj T*
(proportion of the Jews from Austria-Hungary came during the first two) Tj T*
(decades. Throughout, the Jews from Russia have predominated in the) Tj T*
(total movement, governing its course for practically the entire) Tj T*
(period.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the total movement from the three countries of Eastern Europe, the) Tj T*
(Jews have participated most strongly in the Roumanian immigration,) Tj T*
(constituting nine-tenths of this immigration. The Jews are nearly a) Tj T*
(half of the immigrants from Russia. Their participation in the) Tj T*
(immigration from Austria-Hungary is relatively much smaller, being) Tj T*
(less than a tenth of the total immigration. In the immigration of the) Tj T*
(two latter countries, the Jews show a lessening participation, due to) Tj T*
(the great growth of the immigration of the other peoples. In the) Tj T*
(movements from Russia and Roumania, the participation of the Jewish) Tj T*
(immigrants rises greatly in all periods significant in the situation) Tj T*
(of the Jews in these countries. The influence of the unusual) Tj T*
(conditions facing the Jews in Russia and Roumania and of the) Tj T*
(principal events in their history for these thirty years is reflected) Tj T*
(in the annual fluctuations of the Jewish immigration of each of these) Tj T*
(countries to the United States. The economic and social pressure) Tj T*
(exerted upon the Jews in Russia and Roumania is reflected in the) Tj T*
(degree emigration is utilized by them. The Jews from Russia have a) Tj T*
(much higher rate of immigration than any other people immigrating from) Tj T*
(Russia. The rate of immigration of the Jews from Roumania is the) Tj T*
(highest among the Jewish immigrants from Eastern Europe. In both) Tj T*
(annual fluctuations and rate of immigration the movement of the Jews) Tj T*
(from Austria-Hungary does not indicate the existence of special) Tj T*
(influences.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The participation of the Jews in the total immigration to the United) Tj T*
(States is large and increasing in importance. For the last fifteen) Tj T*
(years they formed the second largest body of immigrants. Their fate of) Tj T*
(immigration is also higher than that of any other immigrant people. Of) Tj T*
