stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(these respects--family composition, and small return movement \(both) Tj T*
(indicating permanent settlement\) and in the proportion of skilled) Tj T*
(laborers--the Jewish immigration stands apart even from the "old") Tj T*
(immigration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Further confirmation may be obtained, in the study of the) Tj T*
(characteristics of the Jewish immigration, of the principle) Tj T*
(established in the preceding sections that the rejective forces of) Tj T*
(governmental oppression are responsible for the largest part of this) Tj T*
(immigration. The large family movement of the Jewish immigration is a) Tj T*
(symptom of abnormal conditions and amounts almost to a reversal of the) Tj T*
(normal immigration, in which single or married men without families) Tj T*
(predominate. Even the family movement of the "old" immigrants may) Tj T*
(largely be attributed to the longer residence of their peoples in the) Tj T*
(United States as well as to their greater familiarity with the) Tj T*
(conditions and customs of the United States. That so large a part of) Tj T*
(the Jewish immigrants is composed of dependent females and children) Tj T*
(creates a situation of economic disadvantage for the Jewish) Tj T*
(immigrants, all the stronger because of their relative unfamiliarity) Tj T*
(with the language or the conditions facing them in this country.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Again, the Jews respond slowly and incompletely to the pressure of) Tj T*
(unfavorable economic conditions in this country. This was emphasized) Tj T*
(by the almost complete lack of response to the panic of 1907, as well) Tj T*
(as expressed in the small, practically unchanging return movement of) Tj T*
(the Jews to their European homes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The pressure upon the Jewish artisans, or skilled laborers, in Eastern) Tj T*
(Europe is reflected in the predominance of this class among the Jewish) Tj T*
(immigrants to this country. That so useful an element in Eastern) Tj T*
(Europe with its still relatively backward industrial development--a) Tj T*
(fact that was given express recognition by the permission accorded the) Tj T*
(Jewish artisans in Alexander II's time to live in the interior of) Tj T*
(Russia--should have been compelled to emigrate indicates that the) Tj T*
(voyage across the Atlantic was easier for them than the trip into the) Tj T*
(interior of Russia, access to which is still legally accorded to them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(That the oppressive conditions created particularly in Russia and) Tj T*
(Roumania and operating as a pressure equivalent to an expulsive force) Tj T*
(does not explain the entire Jewish immigration to this country is) Tj T*
(evident from the preceding pages. In a great measure, the immigration) Tj T*
(of Jews from Austria-Hungary is an economic movement. The existence,) Tj T*
(however, of a certain degree of pressure created by economic and) Tj T*
(political antisemitism has however been recognized. The Jewish) Tj T*
(movement from Austria-Hungary shares largely with the movement from) Tj T*
(Russia and Roumania the social and economic characteristics of the) Tj T*
(Jewish immigration which we have described. A strong family movement) Tj T*
(and a relative permanence of settlement, especially as compared with) Tj T*
(the Poles, and a movement of skilled laborers must be predicated of) Tj T*
(the Jewish immigrants from Austria-Hungary, though undoubtedly not to) Tj T*
(the same degree as in the case of the Jewish movements from Russia and) Tj T*
(Roumania.) Tj T*
