() Tj T*
(It is also clear that the forces of economic attraction in the United) Tj T*
(States do not play an altogether passive part in the Jewish) Tj T*
(immigration. The very fact of an immigrant-nucleus formed in this) Tj T*
(country and serving as a center of attraction to relatives and friends) Tj T*
(abroad--a force which increases in direct and multiple proportion to) Tj T*
(the growth of immigration--is an active and positive force in) Tj T*
(strengthening the immigration current. This was early understood by) Tj T*
(the _Alliance Israelite Universelle_ which had acted upon this) Tj T*
(principle in the seventies and had prophetically sought to direct a) Tj T*
(healthy movement of Jewish immigrants to this country in the hope of) Tj T*
(thereby laying a foundation for future Jewish immigration to this) Tj T*
(country. This current, however, once started and growing only by the) Tj T*
(force of its increasing attraction, would reflect in its movement) Tj T*
(almost wholly the economic conditions in this country. That so large a) Tj T*
(part of the Jewish immigration, and so many of the phenomena peculiar) Tj T*
(to it, find their explanation, for the largest part of the thirty) Tj T*
(years, in the situation and the course of events in the countries of) Tj T*
(Eastern Europe leads to the inevitable conclusion that the key to the) Tj T*
(Jewish immigration is to be found not in the force of economic) Tj T*
(attraction exercised in the United States but rather in the) Tj T*
(exceptional economic, social and legal conditions in Eastern Europe) Tj T*
(which have been created as a result of governmental persecution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Reviewing the various phases of the history of Jewish immigration for) Tj T*
(these thirty years, we are enabled to see more closely its nature. The) Tj T*
(study of the immigration, its movement and its social and economic) Tj T*
(characteristics, in comparison with those of other immigrant peoples,) Tj T*
(has revealed in it a number of distinguishing traits. In the causes of) Tj T*
(the emigration of the Jews, in the pressure exerted upon their) Tj T*
(movement as reflected in their rate of immigration, in their family) Tj T*
(movement, in the permanence of their settlement, and in their) Tj T*
(occupational distribution have been found characteristics which mark) Tj T*
(them off from the rest of the immigrant peoples. The number of these) Tj T*
(characteristics and the degree in which they are found in the Jewish) Tj T*
(immigration, put it in a class by itself.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The facts of governmental pressure amounting to an expulsive force,) Tj T*
(and reflected in an extraordinary rate of immigration, in a movement) Tj T*
(of families unsurpassed in the American immigration, the largest part) Tj T*
(economically dependent, in an occupational grouping of skilled) Tj T*
(artisans, able to earn their livelihood under normal conditions, and) Tj T*
(in a permanence of settlement in this country incomparable in degree) Tj T*
(and indicating that practically all who come stay--all these facts) Tj T*
(lead irresistibly to the conclusion that in the Jewish movement we are) Tj T*
(dealing, not with an immigration, but with a migration. What we are) Tj T*
(witnessing to-day and for these thirty years, is a Jewish migration of) Tj T*
(a kind and degree almost without a parallel in the history of the) Tj T*
(Jewish people. When speaking of the beginnings of Russian Jewish) Tj T*
(immigration to Philadelphia, David Sulzberger said: "In thirty years) Tj T*
(the movement of Jews from Russia to the United States has almost) Tj T*
(reached the dignity of the migration of a people," he used no literary) Tj T*
