() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This Government has found occasion to express in a friendly spirit,) Tj T*
(but with much earnestness, to the Government of the Czar its concern) Tj T*
(because of the harsh measures now being enforced against the Hebrews) Tj T*
(in Russia. By the revival of antisemitic laws, long in abeyance, great) Tj T*
(numbers of those unfortunate people have been constrained to abandon) Tj T*
(their homes and leave the Empire by reason of the impossibility of) Tj T*
(finding subsistence within the pale to which it is sought to confine) Tj T*
(them. The immigration of these people to the United States--many other) Tj T*
(countries being closed to them--is largely increasing and is likely to) Tj T*
(assume proportions which may make it difficult to find homes and) Tj T*
(employment for them here and to seriously affect the labor market. It) Tj T*
(is estimated that over 1,000,000 will be forced from Russia in a few) Tj T*
(years. The Hebrew is never a beggar; he has always kept the law--life) Tj T*
(by toil--often under severe and oppressive civil restrictions. It is) Tj T*
(also true that no race, set or class has more fully cared for its own) Tj T*
(than the Hebrew race. But the sudden transfer of such a multitude) Tj T*
(under conditions that tend to strip them of their small accumulations) Tj T*
