(APPENDIX B.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE VII OF THE CONSTITUTION OF ROUMANIA.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Difference in religious beliefs and confessions does not constitute in) Tj T*
(Roumania an obstacle to the obtainment of civil and political rights,) Tj T*
(nor to the exercise of these rights.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(1\) A foreigner without distinction of religion, and whether a subject) Tj T*
(or not of a foreign government, can become naturalized under the) Tj T*
(following conditions:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(a\) He shall address to the government an application for) Tj T*
(naturalization, in which he shall indicate the capital he possesses,) Tj T*
(the profession or craft which he follows, and his abode in Roumania.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(b\) He shall reside, after this application, ten years in the country,) Tj T*
(and prove, by action, that he is of service to it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(2\) The following may be exempted from the intermediary stages:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(a\) Those who have brought into the country industries, useful) Tj T*
(inventions, or talent, or who have founded large establishments of) Tj T*
(commerce or industry.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(b\) Those who, born and bred in Roumania, of parents established in) Tj T*
(the country, have never been subjected, either themselves or their) Tj T*
(parents, to any protection by a foreign power.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(c\) Those who have served under the colors during the war of) Tj T*
(independence; these may be naturalized collectively by government) Tj T*
