(SECRETARY HAY'S NOTE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                                           DEPARTMENT OF STATE, }) Tj T*
(                                 WASHINGTON, _August 11, 1902_. }) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("Excellency:--In the course of an instruction recently sent to the) Tj T*
(Minister accredited to the Government of Roumania in regard to the) Tj T*
(bases of negotiation begun with that government looking to a) Tj T*
(convention of naturalization between the United States and Roumania,) Tj T*
(certain considerations were set forth for the Minister's guidance) Tj T*
(concerning the character of the emigration from that country, the) Tj T*
(causes which constrain it, and the consequences so far as they) Tj T*
(adversely affect the United States.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("It has seemed to the President appropriate that these considerations,) Tj T*
(relating as they do to the obligations entered into by the signatories) Tj T*
(of the Treaty of Berlin, of July 13, 1878, should be brought to the) Tj T*
(attention of the Governments concerned, and commended to their) Tj T*
(consideration in the hope that, if they are so fortunate as to meet) Tj T*
(the approval of the several Powers, such measures as to them may seem) Tj T*
(wise may be taken to persuade the Government of Roumania to reconsider) Tj T*
(the subject of the grievances in question.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("The United States welcomes now, as it has welcomed from the) Tj T*
(foundation of its Government, the voluntary immigration of all aliens) Tj T*
(coming hither under conditions fitting them to become merged in the) Tj T*
(body politic of this land. Our laws provide the means for them to) Tj T*
(become incorporated indistinguishably in the mass of citizens, and) Tj T*
(prescribe their absolute equality with the native born, guaranteeing) Tj T*
(to them equal civil rights at home and equal protection abroad. The) Tj T*
(conditions are few, looking to their coming as free agents, so) Tj T*
(circumstanced physically and morally as to supply the healthful and) Tj T*
(intelligent material of free citizenhood. The pauper, the criminal,) Tj T*
(the contagiously or incurably diseased are excluded from the benefits) Tj T*
(of immigration only when they are likely to become a source of danger) Tj T*
(or a burden upon the community. The voluntary character of their) Tj T*
