(coming is essential; hence we shut out all immigration assisted or) Tj T*
(constrained by foreign agencies. The purpose of our generous treatment) Tj T*
(of the alien immigrant is to benefit us and him alike--not to afford) Tj T*
(to another state a field upon which to cast its own objectionable) Tj T*
(elements. The alien, coming hither voluntarily and prepared to take) Tj T*
(upon himself the preparatory and in due course the definitive) Tj T*
(obligations of citizenship, retains thereafter, in domestic and) Tj T*
(international relations, the initial character of free agency, in the) Tj T*
(full enjoyment of which it is incumbent upon his adoptive State to) Tj T*
(protect him.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("The foregoing considerations, whilst pertinent to the examination of) Tj T*
(the purpose and scope of a naturalization treaty, have a larger aim.) Tj T*
(It behooves the State to scrutinize most jealously the character of) Tj T*
(the immigration from a foreign land, and, if it be obnoxious to) Tj T*
(objection, to examine the causes which render it so. Should those) Tj T*
(causes originate in the act of another sovereign State, to the) Tj T*
(detriment of its neighbors, it is the prerogative of an injured State,) Tj T*
(to point out the evil and to make remonstrance: for with nations, as) Tj T*
(with individuals the social law holds good, that the right of each is) Tj T*
(bounded by the right of the neighbor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("The condition of a large class of the inhabitants of Roumania has for) Tj T*
(many years been a source of grave concern to the United States. I) Tj T*
(refer to the Roumanian Jews, numbering some 400,000. Long ago, while) Tj T*
(the Danubian principalities labored under oppressive conditions, which) Tj T*
(only war and a general action of European powers sufficed to end, the) Tj T*
(persecution of the indigenous Jews under Turkish rule called forth in) Tj T*
(1872 the strong remonstrance of the United States. The Treaty of) Tj T*
(Berlin was hailed as a cure for the wrong, in view of the express) Tj T*
(provisions of its forty-fourth article, prescribing that "in) Tj T*
(Roumania, the difference of religious creeds and confessions shall not) Tj T*
(be alleged against any person as ground for exclusion or incapacity in) Tj T*
(matters relating to the enjoyment of civil and political rights,) Tj T*
(admission to public employments, functions, and honors, or the) Tj T*
(exercise of the various professions and industries in any locality) Tj T*
(whatsoever," and stipulating freedom in the exercise of all forms of) Tj T*
(worship to Roumanian dependents and foreigners alike, as well as) Tj T*
(guaranteeing that all foreigners in Roumania shall be treated, without) Tj T*
(distinction of creed, on a footing of perfect equality.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("With the lapse of time these just prescriptions have been rendered) Tj T*
(nugatory in great part, as regards the native Jews, by the legislation) Tj T*
(and municipal regulations of Roumania. Starting from the arbitrary and) Tj T*
(controvertible premise that the native Jews of Roumania domiciled) Tj T*
(there for centuries are "aliens not subject to foreign protection,") Tj T*
(the ability of the Jew to earn even the scanty means of existence that) Tj T*
(suffice for a frugal race has been constricted by degrees, until) Tj T*
(nearly every opportunity to win a livelihood is denied; and until the) Tj T*
(helpless poverty of the Jew has constrained an exodus of such) Tj T*
(proportions as to cause general concern.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
