288 0 obj
<< /Length 3025 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
("The United States offers asylum to the oppressed of all lands. But) Tj T*
(its sympathy with them in no wise impairs its just liberty and right) Tj T*
(to weigh the acts of the oppressor in the light of their effects upon) Tj T*
(this country and to judge accordingly.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("Putting together the facts now plainly brought home to this) Tj T*
(Government during the past few years, that many of the inhabitants of) Tj T*
(Roumania are being forced, by artificially adverse discriminations, to) Tj T*
(quit their native country; that the hospitable asylum offered by this) Tj T*
(country is almost the only refuge left to them; that they come hither) Tj T*
(unfitted, by the conditions of their exile, to take part in the new) Tj T*
(life of this land under circumstances either profitable to themselves) Tj T*
(or beneficial to the community; and that they are objects of charity) Tj T*
(from the outset and for a long time--the right of remonstrance against) Tj T*
(the acts of the Roumanian Government is clearly established in favor) Tj T*
(of this Government. Whether consciously and of purpose or not, these) Tj T*
(helpless people, burdened and spurned by their native land, are forced) Tj T*
(by the sovereign power of Roumania upon the charity of the United) Tj T*
(States. This Government cannot be a tacit party to such an) Tj T*
(international wrong. It is constrained to protest against the) Tj T*
(treatment to which the Jews of Roumania are subjected, not alone) Tj T*
(because it has unimpeachable ground to remonstrate against the) Tj T*
(resultant injury to itself, but in the name of humanity. The United) Tj T*
(States may not authoritatively appeal to the stipulations of the) Tj T*
(Treaty of Berlin to which it was not and cannot become a signatory,) Tj T*
(but it does earnestly appeal to the principles consigned therein) Tj T*
(because they are the principles of international law and eternal) Tj T*
(justice, advocating the broad toleration which that solemn compact) Tj T*
(enjoins and standing ready to lend its moral support to the fulfilment) Tj T*
(thereof by its co-signatories, for the act of Roumania itself has) Tj T*
(effectively joined the United States to them as an interested party in) Tj T*
(this regard.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
("You will take an early occasion to read this instruction to the) Tj T*
(Minister for Foreign Affairs and, should he request it, leave with him) Tj T*
(a copy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                               "I have the honor to be,) Tj T*
(                                     "Your obedient servant,) Tj T*
(                                                      "JOHN HAY".) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
